      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C05"],
      "claim": "S 38093, an amide with a basic piperidine and ether linkage, rapidly reached brain levels about 10-fold higher than plasma in rats after oral dosing, supporting CNS access for this chemotype.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "M4 PAM 15q, a heteroaromatic amide with basic amine features, showed excellent CNS penetration with a rat Kp of 3.4 in a standard plasma:brain level cassette paradigm.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "A PET radioligand with a cyclopentylpiperazine amide scaffold showed good brain uptake with an SUV of 2.4 in rat PET imaging, further supporting CNS access for N-cyclopentyl amine amide analogues.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Pass: multiple structurally related amide/ether/cyclopentyl-amine CNS agents show direct brain penetration (brain/plasma 1-10, Kp 3.4, PET uptake), outweighing the uncertain physicochemical efflux prior for the query.",
